1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for the sun setting
over the Nakagawa river,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,880
Onto the head of a carpenter
who was busy chopping,

4
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I chase my energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
with one more yawn, nothing really changes.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed-hat water bottle,

9
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:07,440
the vast sky, the sun sinks down.

10
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too,
it will end just like this, won't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,720
Katsushika, Shibamata, happiness again.

12
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:22,440
After running around, I realized it.

13
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:24,540
Because I'm such a fool,

14
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,600
my first love? That's Ryotsu.

15
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:40,340
Chief Ohara, have some tea.

16
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:43,240
Thanks.

17
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:46,380
Holing yourself up to work like
that isn't good for your health.

18
00:01:47,060 --> 00:01:51,060
I've got some work I
really need to finish today.

19
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:54,220
I see. Please don't overdo it.

20
00:01:55,340 --> 00:01:56,360
Thank you, Asada-kun.

21
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:59,920
Don't call me Asada-kun.
Please call me Yūko.

22
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:03,180
R-really? Then... Yū-

23
00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:04,920
Yūko.

24
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:06,200
Yūko.

25
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:10,180
Hey, officer! Hey, officer!
Are you listening?

26
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:13,920
Excuse me, which way do I go to
the bus stop for Yokoyama Station?

27
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:17,420
For the bus stop, if you follow this road...

28
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:18,220
I see.

29
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:32,840
Anyone wishing to buy Yūko Asada's photo book,
on sale today,

30
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:35,840
please line up in this queue to purchase it.

31
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:40,280
Please don't push.
Line up in two rows, in order.

32
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:42,720
We have plenty of copies prepared,

33
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:46,960
but once they sell out, we'll be closing the sale.
Thank you for your understanding.

34
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:48,160
Well, what do we have here!

35
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:51,780
Section Chief, yes. I'll definitely get one.

36
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:52,900
Out of the way, hey!

37
00:02:57,020 --> 00:03:00,630
No, no, this won't do.
The main building is currently

38
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:04,340
on duty. But... but...

39
00:03:04,340 --> 00:03:06,820
Anyone who wants one,
please line up quickly.

40
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:15,240
This is the final day.

41
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:17,980
Those wishing to buy
Yūko Asada's photo book,

42
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:20,400
You'll make it all the way home, right?

43
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:24,720
Thank you very much.

44
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:25,880
Thank you very much.

45
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:28,780
Thank you very much.

46
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:29,880
Thank you very much.

47
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:31,460
Thank you very much.

48
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:33,220
Thank you very much.

49
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:33,860
Thank you very much.

50
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:43,060
Aaaaaaaaaah!

51
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:43,560
Thank you very much.

52
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:45,860
My share.

53
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:46,860
Chief.

54
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:48,440
Thank goodness.

55
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,000
One copy.

56
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,100
No, one copy rather than five.

57
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,080
Thank you very much.

58
00:03:56,260 --> 00:03:57,220
So happy.

59
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:59,440
Chief.

60
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:05,280
Ryotsu, what are you doing here?

61
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,200
It's no use trying to cover it up.

62
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,640
I saw it with my own eyes.

63
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:12,700
A chief like you, during work hours...

64
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:16,300
Well, what's that you're holding there?

65
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:21,300
I was only browsing while
on anti-shoplifting patrol.

66
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,900
Patrol, you say?

67
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:25,060
Now, now, let's not be so stiff about this.

68
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:27,560
In exchange, let me see it too.

69
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:29,160
Whoa, flip back to here.

70
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:32,480
What is this?

71
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:35,260
Isn't it HK?

72
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:37,120
Of course it is.

73
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:39,400
Who do you think Yūko Asada is?

74
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,080
She's really beautiful, isn't she?

75
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:46,060
She's every woman's dream.

76
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:47,660
You can't help but be captivated, can you?

77
00:04:47,660 --> 00:04:51,080
Of all the actresses in Japan,

78
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,820
she's the only one who
could make it internationally.

79
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:54,060
I see.

80
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:55,480
Yeah, that's right.

81
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:58,860
I didn't get a good look at her earlier.

82
00:04:58,860 --> 00:04:59,860
Hey, Ryo-tsu!

83
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:02,000
Don't handle it so roughly!

84
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:05,220
The Chief's taste is surprisingly trendy,
isn't it?

85
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,660
So that means you have no individuality.

86
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,500
Your face is too close.

87
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:13,420
You're spraying spit.

88
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:14,660
Don't crease it.

89
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:16,280
Hold on a moment, please.

90
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:19,440
I've met this actress somewhere before,
you know.

91
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:21,400
With Yuko Asada?

92
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:23,220
Idiots who've seen her on TV

93
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:25,380
all feel like they know her personally.

94
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:27,020
No, that's not it.

95
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:29,460
I'm sure I've met her somewhere before.

96
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:32,800
What could it be?

97
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:34,400
That's a TV station car, isn't it?

98
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:35,880
Yo, what's up!

99
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:44,760
Look, you're always up to something, aren't you?
Don't look at me, I don't know anything, Kan-chan.

100
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:50,380
Well, as expected, he's got character.
He'd be a hit on TV, you know.

101
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:54,800
What's this about TV? Actually, I'm...

102
00:05:55,540 --> 00:06:03,340
I'm a director at KTV, and I came all this
way to get Kan-chan to appear on television.

103
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:05,400
This idiot on TV?

104
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:07,880
Yes, Kan-chan,
you're not so easy to dismiss after all.

105
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:12,060
She'll be thrilled to know her first
love was looking at her photo book.

106
00:06:12,060 --> 00:06:13,700
What are you talking about?

107
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:15,260
Don't play dumb.

108
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:20,020
Can you believe it? Despite being the
first love of the great actress Yūko Asada!

109
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:23,060
Senpai is Yūko Asada's first love, they say!

110
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:26,460
Surely it must be some kind of mistake.

111
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,240
That's right, it's a mistake.

112
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,700
I absolutely won't believe it.

113
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:30,680
No way.

114
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:34,000
KTV, of all stations,
wouldn't make a mistake like that.

115
00:06:34,920 --> 00:06:37,280
We've confirmed the story, Kan-chan.

116
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:37,900
Hey.

117
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:39,720
It's me.

118
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:42,360
from my elementary school photo album.

119
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:45,280
We've checked with Yūko's mom.

120
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,900
Just as expected, she's been posing
for the camera since she was a kid.

121
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:51,220
This is a photo from a school field trip.

122
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:55,380
Now that you mention it, at the kimono
shop behind the elementary school...

123
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:57,560
there was a girl with big eyes.

124
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:58,960
That's right.

125
00:07:02,300 --> 00:07:05,700
So what you said about having met her was true,
after all.

126
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:07,340
Nice one.

127
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:09,191
W-well, I see,

128
00:07:09,241 --> 00:07:13,100
that she had a crush on me, of all people.

129
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:16,640
Her heart fluttering with
a tender maiden's longing,

130
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:18,443
always hiding, my first love,

131
00:07:18,493 --> 00:07:21,020
she watched over her beloved Kan-chan.

132
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:23,920
You're quite the charmer, aren't you?

133
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:24,560
No, no.

134
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:27,700
That Yūko-san, pure as a white robe,

135
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:30,300
a caveman-like guy like this?

136
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:34,680
Unbelievable!
Asking me to believe it is impossible!

137
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:39,240
But I've never even spoken to her once!

138
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:41,840
It was her one-sided crush, after all.

139
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:44,360
We've even looked into some episodes.

140
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:47,620
He was a cool sportsman with long legs,
they said.

141
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:49,640
Long legs?

142
00:07:50,180 --> 00:07:52,360
Even generously speaking, they're not long.

143
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:55,200
Maybe they just looked long
from an optical illusion.

144
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:57,380
His nickname is really wonderful.

145
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,920
Ryotsu's nickname back in
elementary school was...

146
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:03,440
Yeah, it was around this time, I think.

147
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:06,220
It's a perfectly fitting nickname, but

148
00:08:06,220 --> 00:08:07,720
it's hardly a lovely one.

149
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:09,440
Could the data be wrong?

150
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:12,700
KTV, the nation's top network,
wouldn't make a mistake!

151
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:15,280
That's right, this is conclusive evidence!

152
00:08:15,820 --> 00:08:18,820
On graduation day,
I got a love letter in my shoe locker.

153
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:21,300
What, a love letter in a shoe locker?

154
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:24,200
Did something that happy really happen?

155
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,440
You did get one, didn't you?

156
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:40,580
I don't remember, but think back! Remember, remember, remember!
Now that you say it, I feel like I did get one... got one, got one, got one, right?

157
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:47,080
Got it, got it, you got one!
See, our research has no mistakes after all!

158
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:54,340
Yeah, I'm starting to remember.
Wasn't the envelope between the shoes pink?

159
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:56,560
Pink, bingo!

160
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,140
So it was pink after all.

161
00:08:58,740 --> 00:08:59,180
That's right.

162
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:03,620
I'm Yuko Asada's first love.

163
00:09:04,100 --> 00:09:05,120
That settles it.

164
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,740
Well, I'll get in touch with you later.

165
00:09:08,660 --> 00:09:09,100
Thanks.

166
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:12,680
That's amazing, Ryo-chan.

167
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:16,300
Well, Kan-chan, we're close enough that we call each other
"Yu-rin."

168
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:18,180
That great actress, "Yu-rin"?

169
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:20,700
You never know what
might happen in this world.

170
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:24,440
That said, Ryotsu,
I have a favor to ask of you.

171
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:25,880
A favor? What is it?

172
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:30,840
When you see Yuko-san, could you get
her to sign this photo book for me?

173
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:34,620
Make sure she writes "To Ohara, love."

174
00:09:35,340 --> 00:09:39,540
Even if I was her first love,
I can't be that shameless.

175
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:41,980
But please, just this once.

176
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:45,040
If you really insist,
I suppose I could think about it.

177
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,400
I see.

178
00:09:46,400 --> 00:09:50,640
If you copy what I do here,
I'll see what I can do.

179
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,700
When I was in elementary school,
I did this at morning assembly.

180
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:56,420
It's a gag that had the whole
school roaring with laughter.

181
00:09:56,420 --> 00:09:57,760
What is that supposed to be?

182
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,180
That's suspicious.

183
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:02,300
It's Ryo-chan we're talking about,
so it might be a made-up gag.

184
00:10:02,860 --> 00:10:03,960
Good point.

185
00:10:04,420 --> 00:10:06,400
If you don't want to, that's fine.
If you don't want to.

186
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:12,340
Yuko must have been gazing at my gag,
completely entranced, right?

187
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:13,700
Got it.

188
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:16,680
Then I'll definitely
get her autograph, right?

189
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:18,620
Of course, a man's promise.

190
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:22,300
No, not just the autograph,
I'll even scrape them off with you.

191
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:24,700
Then you might even get a handshake.

192
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:25,940
Handshake.

193
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:27,500
Thanks.

194
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:30,080
Alright, I'll do it.

195
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:31,420
How do I do it?

196
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:32,460
First,

197
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:35,020
stick your finger up your nostril.

198
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,620
What are you doing? Hurry up.

199
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:42,080
Hey.

200
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:44,700
Chief's really going for it.

201
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:45,400
No way.

202
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:53,740
W-well, how's this, Ryotsu?
This'll do, right?

203
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:56,400
If you're not really up for it, that's fine.

204
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,480
W-what? Did I get something wrong?

205
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:01,800
The Chief's butt isn't showing!

206
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:03,660
W-what, b-butt!

207
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:06,440
I'm going to see Yuko Asada in person,
the one I've always admired.

208
00:11:07,100 --> 00:11:08,900
We've gotta go this far.

209
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:10,640
I-I get it.

210
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:17,740
Aren't you embarrassed to go that far?

211
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:18,540
What?

212
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:20,920
Just kidding.

213
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:22,140
Understood.

214
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:24,480
Yuko Asada's first love.

215
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:27,060
Leave everything to Kankichi Ryotsu.

216
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,040
Well, I'm off, then.

217
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:33,540
Ohara.

218
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:37,740
Yes, yes.

219
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:41,060
Good work.

220
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:46,260
The Chief's turned into Ryo-chan's manager

221
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:47,560
You're acting like you're in love.

222
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:49,140
It can't be helped.

223
00:11:49,140 --> 00:11:51,940
Thanks to him, I get to meet Yuko Asada,
the woman I've always adored.

224
00:11:58,680 --> 00:11:59,780
It's the TV station!

225
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,440
Look, look, Ryotsu!

226
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:07,460
TV stations really are huge

227
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:08,540
Ryotsu.

228
00:12:08,540 --> 00:12:09,700
It's fine, it's fine.

229
00:12:11,060 --> 00:12:13,220
Could you do a read-through with that director,
Mizusawa?

230
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:15,320
Yo, Kan-chan!

231
00:12:15,780 --> 00:12:16,620
We've been waiting for you!

232
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,520
Yo, Mizusawa!

233
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:19,900
Hoah!

234
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:22,880
Up and down on the Sumop's Omu-tag!

235
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:27,040
Chief, Chief, it's a regular omelet!

236
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:30,340
What? What's this about
the regular matsutake omelet?

237
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:32,920
The Chief wouldn't understand, would he?

238
00:12:32,920 --> 00:12:34,880
That we can't share this emotion together...

239
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:38,280
I've been devoted to Yuko Asada, you know.

240
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:42,060
It's thanks to this first love
that you'll get to meet that Yurin.

241
00:12:42,060 --> 00:12:44,460
Make sure you understand that part, okay?

242
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,120
I get it.

243
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:48,420
Kan-chan, you look sharp today too.

244
00:12:48,840 --> 00:12:51,080
It's always like this,
let's take it easy, easy does it.

245
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:52,480
Is this where Yurin is?

246
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,680
Yurin, the cameras are rolling!

247
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:15,640
The live show starts at three,
so just wait here quietly for now, Kan-chan.

248
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:18,460
Big stars shouldn't be
kept waiting this long

249
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:21,100
That's right, that's right.

250
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:26,400
Trying to fob us off with stale tea?
Can't they at least provide a box lunch?

251
00:13:26,980 --> 00:13:31,480
You know the tonkatsu from Maizuru and
the nori bento from Sutaya are good, right?

252
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:34,660
What's wrong, Chief?

253
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:36,740
I'm just going to the bathroom for a sec.

254
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:40,280
Chief, there's no need to be so nervous.

255
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:41,320
I'm about to burst.

256
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:44,220
That's better.

257
00:13:44,220 --> 00:13:47,060
Honestly, you could at least
go take a leak on your own.

258
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:50,260
I just feel uneasy being alone, you know.

259
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:53,060
This is why these big
places are such a hassle.

260
00:13:53,060 --> 00:13:54,440
Well then.

261
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:54,880
Right.

262
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:55,520
Right.

263
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:56,260
Right.

264
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:03,040
Which way did we come from again?

265
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:04,760
Well, whatever.

266
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:07,560
Wasn't it this way?

267
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:11,560
The Chief's such a worrywart.
Leave it to me, I'll...

268
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:12,740
Was it here?

269
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:16,040
Makeup coming through!

270
00:14:16,920 --> 00:14:18,560
Excuse us, coming through!

271
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:23,660
Hey, hey,
I'm the one who's going out there, you know.

272
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:27,380
So I got the wrong vice?

273
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:30,580
Pull yourself together, Ryotsu.
I'm leaving this to you, you hear?

274
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:33,780
Don't worry. We just have to
get to the studio on time, right?

275
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:36,480
If you get it wrong again,
I won't stand for it.

276
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,120
Don't say things like that.

277
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:40,900
Is it really fine if we
don't get to meet Yuko Asada?

278
00:14:41,820 --> 00:14:42,780
No way, no way.

279
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:45,160
Ryotsu, please don't say that,
I'm begging you.

280
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:46,720
As long as you understand.

281
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,920
Then keep quiet and follow me.

282
00:14:48,920 --> 00:14:50,140
Ryotsu.

283
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:51,480
What's wrong, Ohara?

284
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:52,780
No, it's nothing.

285
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:03,080
Are we really supposed to be here?

286
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:09,240
Chief, we're on camera!

287
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:12,860
Is it this camera?

288
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:15,000
What?

289
00:15:17,620 --> 00:15:19,400
Which one is showing up on TV?

290
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:21,740
This one? This one? This one?

291
00:15:23,380 --> 00:15:24,420
Throw them out!

292
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:27,520
Chief, Chief, look, I'm on camera, right?

293
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:30,020
I don't know you, you're a stranger!

294
00:15:30,020 --> 00:15:30,840
What's wrong?

295
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:34,380
Aaaaah! I'm I'm the -

296
00:15:35,340 --> 00:15:39,300
Who do you think I am?
I'm Yuko's first love!

297
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:43,380
Hahaha! Why do I have to run away too?

298
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:44,720
Aaaaah!

299
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:56,480
Honestly, what a rude person.

300
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:59,940
Something smells delicious.

301
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:05,840
Hello. I'm Kankichi Ryotsu,
Yuko Asada's first love.

302
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:07,700
Is anyone here?

303
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:09,200
Hey!

304
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:13,080
Why is there food in a place like this?

305
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:15,300
They must have used it
for a drama or something.

306
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:20,020
Perfect.
I'm hungry, so let's just dig in ourselves.

307
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:21,920
Isn't that a bad idea?

308
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:24,720
This is good.
Chief, you should eat some too.

309
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:25,800
But...

310
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:30,804
Well then,

311
00:16:30,854 --> 00:16:35,310
Presenting a famous Chinese dish,
the cooking Peking Man.

312
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:37,160
Today's dish is this!

313
00:16:44,240 --> 00:16:45,260
Idiot!

314
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:47,740
I haven't even eaten all of it yet!

315
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:50,740
Never mind that, Ryotsu,
we're running out of time!

316
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:54,240
No way.

317
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:57,840
This is amazing! The Russians,

318
00:16:57,890 --> 00:17:00,700
here's Petti-san,
sparks celebrating on a throne of flames!

319
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:02,940
Hey, Ryotsu, is this spot okay?

320
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:04,520
It's fine right here.

321
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:06,930
Why is it that when you
look at a set from the back,

322
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:09,440
it's just a simple thing made of plywood,
isn't it?

323
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:11,360
Move!

324
00:17:11,660 --> 00:17:11,980
Whoa!

325
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:17,040
Th-th-th-th-th-th...

326
00:17:24,660 --> 00:17:27,080
Why do I always get these looks?

327
00:17:27,080 --> 00:17:30,960
Ryotsu, you're...

328
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:32,700
here you are!

329
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:35,200
What are you doing?
The live show's about to start!

330
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:36,600
Yes.

331
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:40,580
It's about to start.

332
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:42,460
I hope Ryo-chan will be all right.

333
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:44,700
More importantly,
will the Chief be on camera?

334
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,680
My heart is pounding for some reason.

335
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:58,120
Hello, everyone! It's time for
"Gogo no Sanji Yarō"!

336
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:03,360
Today's guest is the popular actress Yuko Asada,
who represents Japan.

337
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:07,620
Yuko Asada really is beautiful, isn't she?

338
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:09,520
When you see her up close...

339
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:16,100
It's almost dazzling.

340
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:20,840
When you meet Ms. Asada,
give her this bouquet, okay?

341
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:26,100
And remember how charming I was as a kid.

342
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:28,200
I guess we can just let
Yuurin do the talking, right?

343
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:30,100
Leave it to me, don't worry.

344
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:34,600
And now,
the long-awaited memory reunion corner!

345
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:36,600
Here we go at last.

346
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:40,260
Come on, Ms. Asada, let's go.

347
00:18:40,260 --> 00:18:42,400
Oh no, my heart's pounding now.

348
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,160
First, the silhouette quiz.

349
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,700
Who could this be?

350
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:51,360
Sorry, but this isn't
quite enough for me to tell.

351
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:55,400
No wonder. After all,
it's different from elementary school.

352
00:18:56,280 --> 00:18:59,129
Then, I'll call Ms. Asada by
her nickname from back then,

353
00:18:59,179 --> 00:19:01,420
so listen carefully. Go ahead!

354
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:03,100
Yu-rin.

355
00:19:03,320 --> 00:19:04,740
I still don't get it.

356
00:19:06,740 --> 00:19:09,940
If she realizes it's me,
Yu-rin is going to be thrilled.

357
00:19:11,660 --> 00:19:13,900
You're Kan-chan!

358
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:17,700
Yu-rin!

359
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:22,020
Yuu-ree... what was it again?

360
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:25,780
What would I do if she said,
"Please marry me"?

361
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:28,520
I'll give you a big hint.

362
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,280
The first part of the surname is "ri."

363
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:32,900
R... Rin.

364
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:37,600
Even in her troubled look,
she's more beautiful than ever.

365
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:40,580
All right, then here's a big hint!

366
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:42,200
Her name is Kankichi.

367
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:44,460
Kankichi-san.

368
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:47,180
Still can't remember?

369
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:49,800
Well, it's because you don't
call me by my full name properly.

370
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:53,780
Hey, hey, what's going on?
Mizusawa-chan, come on, please.

371
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:56,480
It's fine, it's fine!

372
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:58,440
Even the big actress seems to be in a bind

373
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:00,840
Well then, let's go for it.

374
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,380
The full name is...

375
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:13,000
It's Kankichi Ryotsu.

376
00:20:13,640 --> 00:20:15,960
Kankichi Ryotsu?

377
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:19,080
Yes, it's Kankichi Ryotsu.

378
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:20,740
Who?

379
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:25,220
I have a bad feeling about this.

380
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:30,660
Do great actresses forget names even
when they never forget their lines?

381
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,560
After all,
it's been since elementary school.

382
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:37,460
Now, for a super-special treat,
let's bring out the man himself.

383
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:41,300
Even if you forget the name,
you should remember my face.

384
00:20:43,060 --> 00:20:45,200
Kankichi Ryotsu, please come out!

385
00:20:50,560 --> 00:20:51,840
Yu-rin!

386
00:20:52,700 --> 00:20:53,740
Who's this guy?

387
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:56,520
Wh-what ah

388
00:20:56,860 --> 00:20:58,000
What's going on here?

389
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:01,900
His nickname was Funkorogashi.
Now do you remember?

390
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:03,420
Well...

391
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:05,500
"Well" what?

392
00:21:07,460 --> 00:21:10,020
Hey, bring out the photos too.
And the love letter.

393
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:13,236
Well, it has been over twenty years.

394
00:21:13,286 --> 00:21:14,440
Trying to remember it.

395
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:18,840
Uh, I forgot something important.

396
00:21:19,500 --> 00:21:22,460
Ms. Asada, you once put a love
letter in a shoe locker, didn't you?

397
00:21:23,140 --> 00:21:26,360
A love letter? In a shoe locker? Right.

398
00:21:26,780 --> 00:21:28,208
This is the person it was for.

399
00:21:28,258 --> 00:21:31,080
Look at the photos from back then, and
you'll remember whether you like it or not.

400
00:21:32,460 --> 00:21:36,240
This is her. This is Ryo-chan,
the one who gave the love letter.

401
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:38,831
Hey, rather than that,

402
00:21:38,881 --> 00:21:41,520
I think seeing this gag will
bring it back in an instant.

403
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:42,860
G-gag?

404
00:21:42,920 --> 00:21:46,280
That's right! Back then, I was the most
popular kid in the whole school, so...

405
00:21:46,330 --> 00:21:49,740
this was the one-shot routine that swept the entire
school into a whirlwind of laughter at morning assembly!

406
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:51,980
Then, let's have him perform!
Please, go ahead!

407
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:52,860
Nufun!

408
00:21:56,020 --> 00:21:57,460
Apparapara pirāan!

409
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:00,220
I remember now!

410
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:03,380
Yay! It's a touching reunion!

411
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:09,220
Hehehe, right?

412
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:12,613
the one who scribbled on my gym clothes,

413
00:22:12,663 --> 00:22:14,360
the habitual peeping
Tom of the women's bath,

414
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:16,040
Ryotsu Kankichi!

415
00:22:19,380 --> 00:22:20,780
You bloody idiot!

416
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:24,780
B-but Mom said the
person in this photo is...

417
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:28,380
The one I gave the love
letter to is this guy!

418
00:22:28,680 --> 00:22:29,880
Nooooo!

419
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:34,220
Giant, you damn fool, look at him, how
could that guy possibly be Yagami's match!

420
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:34,920
S-s-sorry!

421
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:38,560
This man is the biggest loser in school

422
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:40,120
Ryotsu Kankichi!

423
00:22:41,280 --> 00:22:42,760
Ryotsu Kankichi!

424
00:22:44,380 --> 00:22:45,980
Ryotsu Kankichi!

425
00:22:46,180 --> 00:22:47,640
Ryotsu Kankichi!

426
00:22:52,140 --> 00:22:54,260
Is this going out nationwide?

427
00:22:54,980 --> 00:22:57,460
You idiot!

428
00:23:03,260 --> 00:23:04,360
Apparapara!

429
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:06,820
Ryotsu!

430
00:23:07,300 --> 00:23:08,120
Don't slack off.

431
00:23:08,120 --> 00:23:10,740
Put more force into it!
Give it everything you've got!

432
00:23:10,740 --> 00:23:11,780
Yes, I'm doing it.

433
00:23:11,780 --> 00:23:13,800
Enough already, please let me off.

434
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:15,120
No way.

435
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:18,640
This is payback for
wrecking Yuko Asada's show!

436
00:23:18,640 --> 00:23:19,940
Now then, you lot.

437
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:22,800
Go ahead and take your revenge
for all your pent-up grudges.

438
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:24,240
Yes, sir!

439
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:27,500
Boo-cha!

440
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:31,120
Apura-pura-bira!

441
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:33,300
Apura-pura-bira!

442
00:23:34,320 --> 00:23:36,040
Don't make fun of me!

443
00:23:37,740 --> 00:23:39,680
Hey, thanks for the other day.

444
00:23:39,680 --> 00:23:41,260
You...

445
00:23:41,260 --> 00:23:45,520
Actually, that thing the other
day had the highest ratings.

446
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:48,080
That's the real appeal of live broadcasts,
they say.

447
00:23:48,700 --> 00:23:51,160
So we'd really love for
Kan-chan to appear every day.

448
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:54,300
We're thinking of making a
"Who Are You?" corner.

449
00:23:54,860 --> 00:23:55,880
Don't mess with me!

450
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:59,340
I'm never appearing on TV again!

451
00:24:05,260 --> 00:24:06,540
No matter what anyone says,

452
00:24:06,540 --> 00:24:08,860
I'll put this Wanico collection together.

453
00:24:08,860 --> 00:24:10,680
people tend to misunderstand

454
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:11,700
this guy's character.

455
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:13,560
I can't see him as a stranger at all.

456
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:15,480
And keeping a crocodile

457
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:17,340
has been my dream since I was a kid.

458
00:24:17,700 --> 00:24:20,300
Next time: Wanico,
Tears of a Comedian's Spirit

459
00:24:20,720 --> 00:24:21,360
Take care, okay?

460
00:24:30,420 --> 00:24:37,280
They say I'm a woman who can't fall in love,

461
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:42,940
but I have more things I
want to do than I can count.

462
00:24:44,780 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across the wide desert.

463
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:59,180
I want to be freer than a bird.

464
00:24:59,920 --> 00:25:07,200
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

465
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:15,060
My heart of love, sorry, I give in.

466
00:25:15,060 --> 00:25:22,220
The panoramic future is also dazzling,
and it's coming soon.

467
00:25:23,280 --> 00:25:26,439
You understand, right?

468
00:25:26,489 --> 00:25:30,100
Sorry, just wait for me.

